  "body": "Currently, it requires the URL's scheme to be `https` which is a bit too\nstrict compared to being \"same origin as the secure context where the\nnormalization happens\". For example, it does not allow developers to\nquickly test things using a local http server. It also does not correspond\nto what is implemented in browsers. The condition is relaxed to being an\nHTTP(S) scheme which is good enough given the mentioned requirement of\nbeing \"same origin as the secure context\". An assertion is added to make\nclear this requirement implies that the url is potentially trustworthy.\nThe assertion is handy to see if the normalization algorithm is reused by\nimplementers in a different context.\n\nCloses #5787\n\n<!--\nThank you for contributing to the HTML Standard! Please describe the change you are making and complete the checklist below if your change is not editorial.\n-->\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chrome implements this behavior.\n   * Firefox implements this behavior.\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * This can be tested manually by checking navigator.registerProtocolHandler on a non-https localhost server works.\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chrome: Already implemented.\n   * Firefox: Already implemented.\n   * Safari: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=92726\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/6587/system-state.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 16, 2021, 9:30 AM UTC (6e1c62c)\">/system-state.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/6587/24a6d00...6e1c62c/system-state.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 16, 2021, 9:30 AM UTC (6e1c62c)\">diff</a> )",
